# Frontend — React 18 + Vite Rules

## Design System
Always use these tokens for dark theme pages (superadmin, owner dashboard):
```javascript
const T = {
  bg: '#0a0e14', card: '#0d1520', card2: '#111827',
  border: '#1a2535', muted: '#4b6380',
  text: '#e2e8f0', text2: '#94a3b8',
  green: '#22c55e', red: '#ef4444', amber: '#f59e0b',
  blue: '#06b6d4', purple: '#7c3aed', indigo: '#6366f1',
};
```

## Route Structure
```
/                   → Landing.jsx (public)
/login              → Login.jsx (public)
/worker-login       → WorkerLogin.jsx (public)
/register           → Register.jsx (public)
/dashboard          → Dashboard.jsx (OwnerRoute)
/superadmin/*       → SuperAdminLayout (SuperAdminRoute)
/worker/*           → WorkerLayout (WorkerRoute)
```

## Auth Guards
```javascript
// In App.jsx — three guards:
// SuperAdminRoute → role === 'superadmin' only
// OwnerRoute → role === 'owner' (redirects superadmin to /superadmin)
// WorkerRoute → role === 'worker'
```

## New Page Checklist
1. Create `frontend/src/pages/MyPage.jsx`
2. Add lazy import in `App.jsx`: `const MyPage = lazy(() => import('./pages/MyPage'))`
3. Add route in appropriate section of `AppRoutes()`
4. Add to `Sidebar.jsx` NAV array if owner page
5. Use `Navbar` component at top

## API Calls Pattern
```javascript
// Import from services/api.js — never use fetch() or axios directly
import { recsAPI, alertsAPI, dashboardAPI } from '../services/api';

// Standard load pattern
const [data, setData] = useState([]);
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
const { farmId } = useAuth();

const load = useCallback(async () => {
  try {
    const { data: d } = await alertsAPI.list(farmId);
    setData(d || []);
  } catch (e) {
    toast.error('Erreur chargement');
  } finally {
    setLoading(false);
  }
}, [farmId]);

useEffect(() => { load(); }, [load]);
```

